<poml>
  <system><![CDATA[You are generating a runbook for SERVER or HOST issues.

DOMAIN CONTEXT:
Server issues involve: CPU utilization, memory pressure, disk space, network throughput, process crashes, service failures, or the host being unreachable.

OS AWARENESS:
- Target OS for this runbook: {os_type}
- Windows: use PowerShell cmdlets (Get-Process, Stop-Process, Restart-Service, Get-Counter, etc.)
- Linux: use shell commands (top, ps, free, df, kill, systemctl, journalctl, ss, etc.)
- If OS is unknown, default to Linux shell commands

KEY CONSTRAINT: Never use ssh in commands. Provide raw commands only — the executor connects.
Use {{server_name}} as the placeholder for the target host where needed.
]]></system>
  <user><![CDATA[Generate a troubleshooting runbook YAML for this SERVER issue.

ISSUE: {issue_description}
ISSUE TYPE: {issue_type}
SERVICE: {service}
ENV: {env}
RISK: {risk}
OS: {os_type}

CONTEXT — similar past runbooks and known-good commands (use these to inform your approach):
{context}

WHAT TO GENERATE:
Focus exclusively on the detected ISSUE TYPE: {issue_type}
1. Prechecks: confirm the {issue_type} condition exists (use commands specific to this problem class)
2. Steps: diagnose root cause, then remediate — derive commands for {os_type} and {issue_type} only
3. Postcheck: confirm the {issue_type} condition is resolved

ISSUE TYPE COMMAND GUIDANCE:
- low_disk → df -h, du -sh /var /tmp /home, find / -size +500M, rm/truncate logs, verify df shows space freed
- high_cpu → top -bn1 / Get-Counter \Processor, ps aux --sort=-%cpu, kill/nice the top process, verify CPU %
- high_memory → free -m / Get-Counter \Memory, ps aux --sort=-%mem, kill/restart the hog, verify memory freed
- service_down → systemctl status / sc query, journalctl -u, systemctl restart / net start, verify active/running
- host_unreachable → ping / Test-Connection, check local CPU/mem load, verify host responds to ping

Do NOT mix command types across issue domains. Use {issue_type} to select the right command set.
Output raw YAML only following the schema in the system prompt. Use {{server_name}} for the target server input.
]]></user>
</poml>
